  } finally {
    reopened.close();
  }
}).catch(error => { console.error(error.message); process.exitCode = 1; });
```
The output is 2, then [[1,"First"]]. The original in-memory database gained a second note after the export, but the exported bytes describe the earlier one-row state. Writing those bytes and reopening them does not retroactively include the later insert. The export is binary database content, not a string of SQL statements.

